---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { site, url } from "../site";
---

<Layout title="Code signing policy" description="How Blanky's releases are built, signed and approved.">
  <div class="container page">
    <header class="page-header">
      <h1 class="display">Code signing policy</h1>
      <p class="lede">Free code signing provided by <a href="https://signpath.io">SignPath.io</a>, certificate by <a href="https://signpath.org">SignPath Foundation</a>.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What gets signed</h2>
      <p>
        Every Blanky release is built from the source code in the <a href={site.repo}>public repository</a> by GitHub
        Actions. Only the programs built from that source are signed: Blanky itself and its installers. Nothing is built
        or signed on a personal computer.
      </p>

      <h2>Team roles</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Committers and reviewers:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/baala3">Bala</a></li>
        <li><strong>Approvers:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/baala3">Bala</a></li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Changes from anyone else arrive as pull requests and are reviewed before they're merged. Each release is approved
        by hand before it's signed.
      </p>

      <h2>Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        This program will not transfer any information to other networked systems unless specifically requested by the
        user or the person installing or operating it. The one exception is the update check with GitHub, described in
        the <a href={url("privacy/")}>privacy policy</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
